## Round `initial`

1. Prepare the initial SFT data; report its directory as `replay_data_dir`, the fixer draws replay samples from it.
2. Write `train.py` (one SFT or continuation from a given checkpoint, `--config`, `--data-dir`, `--base-model`, `--output-dir`) and an evaluation script that writes `report.json` with a `score` in [0, 1] and `failures.jsonl`, one JSON object per wrong example with the keys `input`, `expected`, and `produced`.
3. Write a short doc naming the output conventions the evaluation enforces and its exact rendering chain, field by field; report its path as `conventions_path`. The fixer sees only this doc and the failures, never your reasoning.
4. Smoke both scripts on a tiny slice, then run the SFT and evaluate the checkpoint.

## A fix round

The message names the checkpoint to continue from and the fix dataset the fixer built. Continue training from that checkpoint on that dataset for one epoch at learning rate {{ input.continuation_learning_rate }} with the rest of the config unchanged, then evaluate the new checkpoint with the same script.

A crash in your own script is yours to read and fix in this same call.

